Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.12,0:00:07.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those are Ishbalans, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.33,0:00:10.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder what \Nthey're doing here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.72,0:00:14.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The military is with them. \NI'm sure they're under escort.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.63,0:00:18.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This sure is taking a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.14,0:00:22.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard they're having some \Nkind of trouble getting water.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.56,0:00:24.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.91,0:00:28.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That should delay \Ntheir departure a little.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.65,0:00:33.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's a relief. Now we don't have to go all the way to the southern camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.24,0:00:35.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then, what did you guys do?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.90,0:00:37.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You think we did something?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.51,0:00:40.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your pals just suddenly \Nshowed up and grabbed us.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.93,0:00:42.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's awful.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.98,0:00:45.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ishbalans have their \Nown residential areas.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.09,0:00:47.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you leave them \Nand band together,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.45,0:00:49.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you'll make a good target \Nfor the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.21,0:00:55.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By the way, Scar said that the Ishbalans had once created a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.96,0:00:58.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're looking for someone who knows the details about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.91,0:01:01.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys were good friends with Scar-san, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.38,0:01:04.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were {\i1}not{\i0} good friends \Nwith that guy!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.88,0:01:07.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't have anything to tell the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.75,0:01:10.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We do not know anything,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.92,0:01:13.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but there is an old man who \Nlives on the outskirts of Kishua
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.30,0:01:15.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who might know \Nsomething about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.70,0:01:17.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Chief!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.19,0:01:19.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These two should be \Nable to show you where.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.89,0:01:21.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You want us to go there?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.47,0:01:23.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.98,0:01:26.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At least get the children out of here, is that what you're saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.66,0:01:30.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, their information \Nmust come at a cost, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.69,0:01:32.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.57,0:01:35.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is not part of our teachings, \Nbut I don't see how it can be helped.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.23,0:01:37.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Chief...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.93,0:01:41.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll throw in a shower \Nat no extra charge.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.57,0:01:49.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get them outside, \Nor else they'll get cooked!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.55,0:01:58.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.63,0:02:04.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.49,0:02:06.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.14,0:02:07.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.27,0:02:09.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed! Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.65,0:02:10.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hop in!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.49,0:02:13.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry, did you steal that? You can't do that!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.11,0:02:18.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No! They said it's mine if I could fix it. \NWho do they think I am?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.76,0:02:19.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.53,0:02:22.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're out of here!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.00,0:02:36.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.74,0:02:41.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.01,0:02:46.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.74,0:02:53.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.24,0:04:31.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kishua is a bit westward, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.00,0:04:32.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No problem, no problem!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.40,0:04:34.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This sure will help, huh, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.03,0:04:38.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry, how long are you \Nplanning to tag along with us?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.75,0:04:40.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's this now, \Nout of the puny?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.46,0:04:42.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's "out of the blue"!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.51,0:04:46.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What I mean is, \Ngo home already.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.07,0:04:49.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I'm not around, \Nwho's going to fix your Automail?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.60,0:04:51.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's hard on me too.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.29,0:04:55.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wanted to return that child homunculus' arm and leg to Brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.73,0:04:57.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,even if it meant \Nyanking them off of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.97,0:05:01.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I couldn't do that \Nin front of you, Winry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.03,0:05:03.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You couldn't do that \Nin the first place.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.54,0:05:06.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, Al, you couldn't do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.11,0:05:10.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I could, if it was \Nto achieve our goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.12,0:05:11.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.26,0:05:13.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A long time ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.60,0:05:16.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there was this guy who said it was simple for someone to kill another person.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.29,0:05:20.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And indeed, even though it was unavoidable,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.57,0:05:25.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I allowed an alchemist named Majhal to die, long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.47,0:05:28.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was an accident. \NYou were trying to save him, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.25,0:05:32.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And in the 5th Laboratory, \NI nearly killed all of those prisoners.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.46,0:05:37.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Their lives seemed to pale in comparison with Al's body.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.98,0:05:39.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.98,0:05:42.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you couldn't do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.88,0:05:45.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then there's Scar...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.83,0:05:48.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he stands in my way again,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.55,0:05:51.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then, like I did to Greed, \NI'm going to...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.14,0:05:52.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kill him?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.81,0:05:54.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you going to kill that guy?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.35,0:05:56.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But that's the man who...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.07,0:05:58.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That traitor deserves to be killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.54,0:06:04.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any event, \Nour dangerous battle goes on.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.64,0:06:06.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't have anyone \Nslowing us down.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.86,0:06:11.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.77,0:06:14.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll see if I slow you down!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.03,0:06:31.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's as though \Nthere was a war here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.74,0:06:34.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've never even seen a war.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.95,0:06:36.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.81,0:06:40.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We have. \NThis is just like that day...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.33,0:06:42.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the day our mom died.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.89,0:06:45.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The military people \Nsurrounded the city,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.27,0:06:48.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but we didn't \Neven do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.22,0:06:52.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, why did they...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.70,0:06:56.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom! Mom!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.65,0:06:56.89,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,R-Rick!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.89,0:06:57.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.73,0:06:59.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rick! Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.86,0:07:03.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.21,0:07:17.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.26,0:07:19.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't want to go \Nto that defiled place.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.10,0:07:23.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay then, Winry...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.14,0:07:29.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pardon us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.20,0:07:33.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.36,0:07:37.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.49,0:07:39.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's just like the one on Scar-san's right arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.77,0:07:42.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As well as the one under the 5th Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.48,0:07:46.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You two, come on out!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.73,0:07:52.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant! Don't start shooting out of nowhere like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.38,0:07:55.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I figured you would \Nbe able to dodge it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.54,0:07:58.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you knew it was us in the \Nfirst place, then don't shoot!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.84,0:08:01.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was for \NSergeant Fuery's bruise.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.19,0:08:10.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's all right. We'll wait for Ed and Al here, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.30,0:08:13.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where's the Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.55,0:08:16.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He went back to Central \Nwith Warrant Officer Falman.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.43,0:08:20.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So after putting on this sort of display, he ran right back home, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.79,0:08:24.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't abide the way the Colonel acted against the Ishbalans,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.10,0:08:26.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so you attacked the escort train?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.02,0:08:32.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, but right now, it's not as though the Ishbalans are starting any wars,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.65,0:08:35.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so you don't have to go around using force to control them.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.30,0:08:36.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't misunderstand.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.95,0:08:39.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There weren't any fatalities \Namong the Ishbalans this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.81,0:08:42.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was one former \Nsoldier who died.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.13,0:08:44.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A man named Yoki, \Nwhom you two knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.29,0:08:47.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yoki? That old guy is dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.25,0:08:51.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There were shots fired from the Ishbalan side, and Yoki was hit.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.88,0:08:54.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tensions flared as a result.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.28,0:09:03.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Colonel stepped forward, \Nand with a display of his power,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.52,0:09:05.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he dashed the \NIshbalan's will to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.05,0:09:10.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he hadn't done that, there would have been more casualties on both sides.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.28,0:09:15.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not a bad piece of work \Nfor a soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.18,0:09:18.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you discriminating against him \Nbecause he's a soldier?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.39,0:09:20.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're a member of \Nthe military too, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.70,0:09:26.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've decided to move most of \Nthe people to the camp in the south.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.65,0:09:31.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we have to determine who it was that fired first and punish them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.36,0:09:34.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to do that, we're still having several of them remain here.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.97,0:09:39.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's an old man among them, right? The one who lived in that shack.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.00,0:09:47.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is pretty tightly secured here, huh? \NIs he a material witness?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.77,0:09:51.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, the old man is not a suspect. We're just protecting him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.92,0:09:53.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Protecting him?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.79,0:09:59.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those are the Ishbalans \Nwho are under arrest, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.65,0:10:03.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They attacked him. Called him a heretic and an outcast.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.82,0:10:07.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Apparently, he's not \Nregarded as being Ishbalan.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.25,0:10:12.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's ridiculous! I mean, the Ishbalans have always suffered discrimination!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.75,0:10:15.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, even among themselves...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.77,0:10:17.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Outcasts?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.43,0:10:19.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What kind of people are they?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.50,0:10:21.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're defiled.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.23,0:10:23.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're people who have disobeyed the teachings of Ishbala.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.84,0:10:27.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He has a tattoo on his face. \NThat is the mark of an outcast.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.74,0:10:31.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When you say they disobey the teachings, what exactly?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.14,0:10:35.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's what Mom told us.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.35,0:10:38.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Believe in the god Ishbala.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.86,0:10:41.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Otherwise, you'll become an outcast.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.30,0:10:47.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I didn't know that \Nhe was an outcast too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.29,0:10:48.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"He"?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.82,0:10:51.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The one that you call Scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.36,0:10:52.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's an outcast!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.09,0:10:54.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's a traitor!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.58,0:10:59.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What kind of person \Nwas your mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.41,0:11:04.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know, she was very nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.31,0:11:06.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even though her eyes were unwell,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.28,0:11:09.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}she worked for everyone, in a hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.22,0:11:11.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}In a hospital?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.49,0:11:15.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}The Philosopher's Stone, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.23,0:11:18.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the third time \NI've been asked about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.47,0:11:19.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The third time?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.61,0:11:21.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That scarred young man,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.96,0:11:26.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and long ago, his older brother asked me the same question.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.37,0:11:29.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scar and his brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.07,0:11:32.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then Scar's brother created \Na Philosopher's Stone before?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.99,0:11:33.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.03,0:11:38.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He did not make one. \NThe young man was too humane.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.13,0:11:43.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But why do you know about the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.14,0:11:45.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're an Ishbalan, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.12,0:11:50.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am an outcast. \NI learned the Grand Art.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.43,0:11:52.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Grand Art?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.91,0:11:56.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once, we Ishbalans
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.42,0:12:00.26,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,had a secret art that had been passed down, \Nwhich we called the Grand Art.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.26,0:12:03.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And with it, we lived \Nin the lap of luxury.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.13,0:12:06.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, at some point, the art was sealed away
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.39,0:12:09.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and became something \Nforbidden to touch upon.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.19,0:12:12.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who set their hand to it \Nwere made outcasts
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.76,0:12:16.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and were unable to \Nreturn to their homeland.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.86,0:12:21.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Grand Art allowed one to \Nalter the form of all things at will.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.59,0:12:25.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This act was said to be in \Ndefiance of God's teachings.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.34,0:12:29.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then the Grand Art is alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.59,0:12:32.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ridiculous! That's not possible!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.07,0:12:34.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way that Ishbalans,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.53,0:12:39.73,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,who live in the desert and have no \Nmechanical civilization, could have alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.73,0:12:41.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that what you're thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.21,0:12:45.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's nothing to be ashamed of.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.36,0:12:48.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When someone's skin and eye color are different,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.70,0:12:53.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,not thinking that they could be \Nthe same as you are goes both ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.79,0:13:00.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would you mind telling us about how to produce a Philosopher's Stone as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.33,0:13:05.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I doubt that the theory \Nthat you have arrived at
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.83,0:13:09.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and our own ancient art are all that different.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.96,0:13:13.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All that remains is the number of humans sacrificed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.73,0:13:15.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Human... sacrifice?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.86,0:13:20.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A city, or a nation...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.65,0:13:25.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When they fall, there is resentment and blood
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.40,0:13:30.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,of tens or hundreds of thousands of people, as they die mortified.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.79,0:13:36.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When they are taken into \Nthe body of a superior practitioner,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.29,0:13:38.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,a Philosopher's Stone is produced.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.68,0:13:45.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's just an overblown version of \Nthe way that we know how to make one.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.75,0:13:47.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not the one \Nwe're hoping to learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.15,0:13:50.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what about Scar-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.63,0:13:53.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said he was going to make a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.60,0:13:57.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why did you teach \Nmy brother about this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.51,0:14:02.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My brother only wanted to bring the woman he loved back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.66,0:14:04.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But in order for that to happen,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.04,0:14:08.11,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,the Ishbalan people would have to be destroyed, and their lives offered in sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.36,0:14:10.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When my brother realized this, \Nhe blamed himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.37,0:14:12.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said it was as though \Nhe were the one
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.39,0:14:14.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who had summoned the disasters that had beset Ishbal!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.66,0:14:18.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here he is!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.34,0:14:18.67,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,In here!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.86,0:14:29.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't! \NNot with that many of them!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.35,0:14:34.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this scene to repeat itself \Nover and over?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.85,0:14:38.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Will the people of Ishbal \Never obtain eternal peace?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.43,0:14:44.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I can obtain a power \Nbeyond theirs...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.03,0:14:45.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Philosopher's Stone...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.77,0:14:47.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You would become an outcast?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.37,0:14:55.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I already {\i1}am{\i0} an outcast.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.79,0:14:58.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are tens of thousands of lives \Ndwelling within this arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.50,0:15:00.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An outcast?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.40,0:15:02.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A defiled person?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.29,0:15:08.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rick!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.71,0:15:11.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Those who receive pain can still sleep."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.85,0:15:15.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Those who give pain cannot sleep."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.68,0:15:18.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, as of today, \NI shall not sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.06,0:15:23.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go ahead! Go anyplace else but here, you outcast!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.25,0:15:36.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're sure... \Nthey were named Rockbell?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.70,0:15:37.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.81,0:15:39.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was a lady doctor
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.63,0:15:43.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who was scary when she got mad but used to give us candy a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.07,0:15:46.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They would treat anyone, \Neven Ishbalans.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.75,0:15:50.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom said it was awful \Nthat they got killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.83,0:15:54.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You say they were killed by a State Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.57,0:15:57.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They say he was an alchemist who used flame.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.48,0:15:59.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He got a commendation for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.84,0:16:01.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom cried over it, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.24,0:16:06.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,M-Miss!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.14,0:16:10.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The wounds didn't have \Nany burns around them?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.44,0:16:12.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No. What's more, \Nif they had been bullet wounds,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.71,0:16:16.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the entry wounds should be larger than the exit wounds, but they aren't.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.16,0:16:19.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, these are...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.24,0:16:22.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a lieutenant colonel in Central named Archer, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.58,0:16:25.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's going after these guys that are called homunculi.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.16,0:16:26.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homunculi?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.84,0:16:29.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,One of them is a monster that can quickly extend her fingers, like thin spears,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.56,0:16:31.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and then quickly retract them back to normal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.44,0:16:33.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The thickness is about right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.18,0:16:37.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Col. Archer or Major Armstrong would believe this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.93,0:16:39.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It wasn't an Ishbalan.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.01,0:16:46.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't very well ignore the word of \Nan esteemed State Alchemist, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.37,0:16:48.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.06,0:16:49.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yow-ow-ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.57,0:16:52.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.41,0:16:58.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rick, Leo, I managed to get them to overlook anything you might have done.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.85,0:17:03.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more, the people who are \Nbeing held here will not be punished.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.16,0:17:05.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They are going to be \Nsent to the camp, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.12,0:17:09.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you guys want, you can go live in Resembool.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.67,0:17:12.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, we'll go to the camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.30,0:17:13.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.45,0:17:17.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where are you two going?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.00,0:17:18.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to go after Scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.16,0:17:21.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we don't, something terrible is going to happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.81,0:17:22.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Will you kill him?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.81,0:17:24.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why would I?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.83,0:17:26.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because he's an outcast!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.11,0:17:29.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's defiled! That's why!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.02,0:17:32.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We want to stop him.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.68,0:17:34.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, we're alchemists, \Njust like he is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.92,0:17:37.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, we're human.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.38,0:17:40.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We won't kill anyone, and we don't want to let him kill anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.53,0:17:43.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're lying! \NYou hate Ishbalans!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.28,0:18:00.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does this scare you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.53,0:18:02.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not even a little!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.05,0:18:06.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well... I'm a little bit \Nafraid of your red eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.06,0:18:11.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The first time I met Scar, he was \Nthe first Ishbalan I had ever seen,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.68,0:18:13.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so I was more afraid of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.62,0:18:15.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.07,0:18:18.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there are times when \Nour feelings are wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.98,0:18:24.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What your mother and father told you isn't necessarily completely true.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.65,0:18:26.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.48,0:18:28.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we all have to find our own answers for ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.67,0:18:31.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,One step at a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.78,0:18:38.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry, listen...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.93,0:18:40.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That being the case—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.21,0:18:43.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.05,0:18:45.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hawkeye-san, could you take me with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.64,0:18:49.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been so long, and I'd like to see Hughes-san and Elicia-chan.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.89,0:18:50.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.15,0:18:53.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry, has something happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.61,0:19:03.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well then, first up is Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.77,0:19:07.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I sure hope Scar-san hasn't \Nmade his Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.11,0:19:07.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.27,0:19:12.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sounds so strange, \Nus hoping for such a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.72,0:19:15.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What does this switch do?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.30,0:19:27.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.71,0:19:29.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Riza is fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.92,0:19:32.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Riza-san, have you ever shot anyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.12,0:19:37.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, I have. Many times.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.81,0:19:40.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you know any doctors by the name of Rockbell?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.87,0:19:41.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.71,0:19:46.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not sure what you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.82,0:19:51.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but there are times when a soldier has \Nno choice but to take another person's life.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.44,0:19:54.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even when they're following orders that are irrational.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.00,0:19:58.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe that's why I don't like soldiers very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.65,0:20:00.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you're in the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.07,0:20:03.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's because there is \Nsomeone I need to protect.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.76,0:20:06.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is the one thing that \Nnobody has forced me to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.87,0:20:08.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's something I decided myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.64,0:20:13.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I pull this trigger of my own will, \Nfor the sake of the one I need to protect.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.29,0:20:16.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Until the day when \Nthat person achieves his goal,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.78,0:20:19.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will not hesitate \Nto pull this trigger.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.72,0:20:22.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What if that person \Nwas not worth protecting?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.11,0:20:25.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is something else \Nfor me to decide.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.95,0:20:32.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This boy is Wrath. \NHe is the seventh.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.33,0:20:33.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wrath?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.69,0:20:35.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nice to meet you, Wrath.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.04,0:20:41.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want you to go after the \NFullmetal brothers once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.60,0:20:46.05,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Didn't you tell us that there was little hope of making them create a Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.36,0:20:49.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The two of them \Nare heading for Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.06,0:20:50.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.14,0:20:53.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If those boys learn the facts about what happened there,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.52,0:20:57.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they will never think again about making a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.51,0:21:00.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That will make it harder for us to move from here on as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.82,0:21:03.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then can I eat them?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.57,0:21:08.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe. Depending on the circumstances, it might be quicker to dispose of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.50,0:21:25.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. I didn't know anything about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.10,0:21:28.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"I'm going to push him all the way to the top."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.90,0:21:30.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what he \Nalways used to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.96,0:21:33.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was sure he was going to make Mustang-san the Führer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.21,0:21:36.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This can't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.05,0:21:40.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I suppose he did \Nhelp out to that end.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.06,0:21:47.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This can't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.90,0:21:50.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This can't be...
Dialogue: 4,0:23:39.40,0:23:41.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 4,0:23:41.60,0:23:44.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 37: "The Flame Alchemist,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.86,0:23:48.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Fighting Lieutenant, \NThe Mystery of Warehouse 13"
